    {
      "id": "SHELL-ADJACENCY-ASYMMETRIC-DIRECT-INPUT-95E",
      "status": "newly assessed source-level conditional public-input question; actual caller, policy and unique-count reconciliation open",
      "condition": "A direct caller passes particle_count 2 and adjacency lists [[1], []] to SelfCollision::new, then records two distinct dynamic particles inside a usable positive interaction diameter with a correctly built and ordered grid. The list count is valid but the reciprocal relation is absent. No such product caller, object, shader execution, or result was observed.",
      "producer_to_consumer": "The constructor checks only list cardinality before flattening the lists into native buffers. WGSL is_connected(index, other) consults only the current index\u2019s list; under the stated lists it suppresses 0\u21921 but does not suppress 1\u21920. The native source therefore permits unequal pair treatment if this raw direct input is intended to describe a symmetric mesh-edge relation. The ordinary Shell::new first validates the mesh, then ShellMesh::adjacency calls the helper which inserts both directions for each edge/seam.",
      "relationship": "059 q622 explicitly leaves adjacency membership and native consumer open; the historical 774 REG122/ADD122 identified adjacency ingress but do not demonstrate the asymmetric pair in these records. Related to earlier /root/rig_identity SHELL-MESH-DIRECT-ADJACENCY-ENDPOINT-95E, which concerns out-of-range direct helper indexing, not automatically the same first contract or unique finding.",
      "future_repair_direction": "Decide whether arbitrary directed exclusion lists are a supported API or whether this boundary owns a symmetric valid graph; if symmetry is required, construct or validate it coherently before flattening. Preserve valid empty lists, ordinary mesh edges/seams and independent contact modes.",
