    {
      "id": "L12-CLOSURE-SELFCOLLISION-REASON-FACETS",
      "classification": "059 q3439 source contract and previously recorded built-before-dispatch condition, current independent extension only; zero automatic count.",
      "observation": "The constructor adjacency-count and record over-capacity diagnostics have separate predicates. The historical 919 source read already noted built becomes true before fallible dispatch and that the ordinary SubstepHook always forces rebuild. Current source shows the flag set before hash, sort, range and collision recording; KernelBatch records into an encoder and exposes submit separately. If a build attempt returns Err or its distinct batch is not submitted/ordered before a later rebuild=false reuse, the flag alone does not establish a usable completed grid. Same-batch properly ordered recording can be valid; actual dispatch failure, direct caller, submission ordering and native outcomes remain unobserved.",
      "future_repair_direction": "Decide API ownership of grid validity and command-batch lifetime; make any cached-state authority reflect the established ordering/commit contract and preserve intentional same-batch reuse, disabled and count<2 no-ops.",
